WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.235
-Today Dr. Christine Blasey Ford

00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:05.471
testified to the Senate
about the allegations

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:06.739
of sexual assault against

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:08.374
Supreme Court nominee
Brett Kavanaugh.

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:10.743
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:15.214
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:17.449
Coming into this hearing today,
President Trump's aides

00:00:17.449 --> 00:00:18.985
desperately tried
to restrain him

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.987
and prevent him
from attacking Dr. Ford,

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.622
but Trump very quickly
dispensed with that advice

00:00:23.622 --> 00:00:25.091
and went on the offensive.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:27.059
In fact, Trump was
apparently so frustrated

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:29.194
by the growing crisis
around his nominee

00:00:29.194 --> 00:00:32.432
that he decided to take matters
into his own hands.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.733
-President Trump is not only

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:36.168
still standing by
Judge Brett Kavanaugh,

00:00:36.168 --> 00:00:37.937
but tonight,
he's taking the reins

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.707
of defending the embattled
Supreme Court nominee.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.475
He's grown increasingly
dissatisfied

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.477
with how Kavanaugh
has defended himself,

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:45.678
CNN has learned.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:46.846
-The president believes

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.447
on the eve
of this hearing in the Senate

00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:51.317
that he and he, alone,
can put the best spin on this,

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.319
that he can defend his nominee.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:54.487
-Oh, good.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:57.556
Trump is taking charge now.

00:00:57.556 --> 00:00:59.358
That's like if
your computer froze

00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:02.995
and your grandpa was like,
"Let me see that thing.

00:01:02.995 --> 00:01:07.366
You probably just need
more water in the keyboard."

00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:09.702
That's why Trump held his insane
press conference yesterday.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.170
He actually thought
he was helping

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.906
when, for example,
he went off on an insane

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:15.575
and totally unrelated tangent

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.944
about how the Chinese
think he's smart.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.545
-If you look at Mr. Pillsbury,

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:23.782
the leading authority on China,
he was on a good show --

00:01:23.782 --> 00:01:26.352
I won't mention the name
of the show -- recently.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:30.957
And he was saying that China has
total respect for Donald Trump

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:35.528
And for Donald Trump's
very, very large a-brain.

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:38.398
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:46.305
I'm a-sorry?

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:48.440
Why is he doing
a bad Italian accent?

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:51.177
Is he quoting a China expert,
or Super Mario?

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:53.345
[ As Mario ] It's me, a-Mario.

00:01:53.345 --> 00:01:57.250
Donald Trump has a large brain.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.652
Also, I think he's quoting
someone he saw on cable news

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:00.987
named Mr. Pillsbury,

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:03.656
but I also feel like
there's a decent chance

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:08.594
he just saw a commercial
with the Pillsbury Doughboy

00:02:08.594 --> 00:02:12.131
and then he hallucinated
that it was talking to him.

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:14.634
-You have a very,
very large brain.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.636
Hoo-hoo-hoo!

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.237
-[ As Trump] Thank you,
Mr. Pillsbury,

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:22.341
for your kind words
and your delicious biscuits.

00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:24.209
[ Normal voice ] In fact,
Trump's frantic paranoid attempt

00:02:24.209 --> 00:02:26.346
to defend his embattled
Supreme Court nominee

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:29.115
from sexual-assault allegations
led him to a truly crazy place.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.717
Somehow, he found a way

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:33.953
to drag George Washington
into his mess.

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:38.624
-Look, if we brought
George Washington here,

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:40.793
and we said,
"We have George Washington,"

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.361
the Democrats would
vote against him.

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:43.896
Just so you understand.

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:46.432
-I mean,
does he still own slaves?

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.500
Then, yeah.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.170
Democrats would
vote against him,

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.770
And Republicans
would probably say,

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:57.476
"Hey, man, everybody owned
a few slaves in college.

00:02:57.476 --> 00:03:01.547
You want to ruin his life
over it?"

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:04.350
Trump actually kept going
because then he seemed to imply

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.419
that George Washington
had something nefarious

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:08.221
in his background
that we don't know about.

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:10.956
-And he may have had a bad past.
Who knows, you know?

00:03:10.956 --> 00:03:14.961
He may have had some...
I think, accusations made.

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.796
Didn't he have a couple things
in his past?

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:18.631
-Wait.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.199
Did Trump just imply

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:24.370
that George Washington was
as shady as he is?

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.538
"I hear he chopped down
a cherry tree

00:03:26.538 --> 00:03:30.710
and then he used that tree
to pay off a porn star."

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:33.379
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.248
[ Applause ]

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.553
Only Trump.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.288
Only Trump would try
to defend himself

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.923
by slandering another president.

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.391
"So what if I cheated
on my wife?

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:48.594
Abraham Lincoln left his wife
right in the middle of play."

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:50.296
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:52.465
"What? what happened?
Oh, okay.

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:56.669
I didn't read the whole book."

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:58.871
So Trump and Republicans
had already made clear

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:01.273
that their intent
was to protect Kavanaugh

00:04:01.273 --> 00:04:02.574
and dismiss Dr. Ford.

00:04:02.574 --> 00:04:03.876
And in the hearing today,

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:05.511
Republicans picked up
right where Trump left off.

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:07.447
Before Dr. Ford even
uttered a single word,

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:08.881
Iowa senator Chuck Grassley

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.483
delivered
an exhausting monologue

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.518
defending Kavanaugh
and slamming Democrats.

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:14.987
And then after ranting
for almost 15 minutes,

00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:17.790
Senator Grassley finally
turned the mic over

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.358
to the senior Democrat
on the committee,

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:20.627
Dianne Feinstein.

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:23.128
Only to interrupt her
one minute later.

00:04:23.128 --> 00:04:25.464
-Before you get
to your testimony,

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:28.166
and the chairman chose
not to do this,

00:04:28.166 --> 00:04:29.335
I think it's important

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:32.038
to make sure
you're properly introduced.

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:34.072
-By the way, I was
going to introduce her,

00:04:34.072 --> 00:04:35.508
but if you want
to introduce her,

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:36.942
I'll be glad
to have you do that.

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:38.911
But I want you to know
I didn't forget to do it,

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:42.247
because I would do that
just as she was about to speak.

00:04:42.247 --> 00:04:44.617
-You said I didn't do it,
but I'm going to do it.

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:46.785
And then you did it

00:04:46.785 --> 00:04:50.590
and now I can't do it
because it's done.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.658
Dude, shut up.
Your time is up.

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:54.793
You don't get to pop up
out of your coffin

00:04:54.793 --> 00:04:58.864
whenever you want,
like The Crypt-Keeper.

00:04:58.864 --> 00:05:01.734
I was going to do it,
then you did it!

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.470
[ Applause ]

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.440
And yet the Republicans'

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.475
constant sniping
and their obvious attempts

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:11.744
to obstruct the process
and brush Ford aside

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:14.246
did not deter her in any way.

00:05:14.246 --> 00:05:17.717
Her testimony today was
a towering act of courage

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:19.284
given the trauma she's survived.

00:05:19.284 --> 00:05:22.622
Her grace and composure
under unimaginable pressure

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:25.558
which she owed no one
was stunning.

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:27.994
In fact, at one point, Dr. Ford,
a research psychologist,

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:31.364
literally explained to the panel
how memory works.

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:36.502
-How are you so sure
that it was he?

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.103
-The same way that I'm sure

00:05:38.103 --> 00:05:39.872
that I'm talking to you
right now.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:42.675
Just basic memory functions.

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:48.447
And also just the level
of norepinephrine

00:05:48.447 --> 00:05:49.848
and epinephrine
in the brain

00:05:49.848 --> 00:05:53.819
that sort of, as you know,
encodes that neurotransmitter,

00:05:53.819 --> 00:05:56.288
encodes memories
into the hippocampus.

00:05:56.288 --> 00:05:58.057
-She's in the middle
of testifying

00:05:58.057 --> 00:06:00.292
in the intense glare
of the national spotlight

00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:01.894
about an alleged sexual assault

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:03.462
committed by
a Supreme Court nominee

00:06:03.462 --> 00:06:06.698
and she just taught everyone
how the brain works.

00:06:06.698 --> 00:06:09.735
She gave a detailed anatomy
of the hippocampus

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:11.136
and the memory centers
in the brain

00:06:11.136 --> 00:06:15.307
to a roomful of guys
who look like they eat brains.

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:17.175
Seriously, just think about --

00:06:17.175 --> 00:06:19.311
Think about how impressive
that is.

00:06:19.311 --> 00:06:21.046
She's a research psychologist

00:06:21.046 --> 00:06:22.348
explaining how the mind works

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:24.183
in the middle
of a horrific experience

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:26.185
that no one should
ever have to endure.

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:27.519
Meanwhile, the most
coherent thing

00:06:27.519 --> 00:06:30.389
Trump has ever said about
the mind is that he has a...

00:06:30.389 --> 00:06:33.292
-Very, very large a-brain.

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:34.326
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.326 --> 00:06:36.095
-in fact, throughout
the hearing --

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:37.597
Throughout the hearing,

00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:39.999
Republicans really had to scrape
the bottom of the barrel

00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:41.567
to try to discredit Dr. Ford.

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:44.170
At one point, the prosecutor
Republicans picked

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:45.705
went down a confusing
line of questioning

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:47.439
about Dr. Ford's fear of flying,

00:06:47.439 --> 00:06:49.608
Republicans have also
spent weeks falsely implying

00:06:49.608 --> 00:06:52.044
that Dr. Ford was missing
key facts in her story.

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:54.413
But throughout this hearing,
it became clear that they were

00:06:54.413 --> 00:06:55.847
the ones who had
basic facts wrong,

00:06:55.847 --> 00:06:58.684
like when they asked her
about her travels to Australia.

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:00.252
-In fact, you fly

00:07:00.252 --> 00:07:02.088
fairly frequently
for your hobbies,

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:04.189
and you've had to fly
for your work.

00:07:04.189 --> 00:07:07.460
Is that true?
-Correct. Unfortunately.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:10.495
-You were a consulting
biostatistician

00:07:10.495 --> 00:07:11.697
in Sydney, Australia.

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:14.566
Is that right?
-I've never been to Australia.

00:07:14.566 --> 00:07:17.570
But the company I worked for
is based in Australia.

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:20.373
-"You said you flew to Australia
to eat dinner?"

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:23.643
"Uh, no, I said I went
to an Outback Steakhouse."

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:26.112
[ Laughter ]

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:33.919
[ Applause ]

00:07:33.919 --> 00:07:36.389
And if you thought
the Republican attacks --

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:38.524
If you thought
the Republican attacks

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:40.259
couldn't get any dumber
and more desperate,

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:41.661
you were wrong
because you forgot

00:07:41.661 --> 00:07:43.663
that there's a second
Donald Trump.

00:07:43.663 --> 00:07:45.364
And he chimed in on Twitter

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:46.799
after the airplane question
to say this --

00:07:46.799 --> 00:07:50.035
"I'm no psychology professor,
but it does seem weird to me

00:07:50.035 --> 00:07:52.504
that someone could have
a selective fear of flying."

00:07:52.504 --> 00:07:54.573
Oh!

00:07:54.573 --> 00:07:58.911
Oh, you're not
a psychology professor?

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:01.447
Is that why you look
like a princess kissed

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:02.948
a double-parked BMW,

00:08:02.948 --> 00:08:06.518
and it came to life?

00:08:06.518 --> 00:08:10.122
Well, Dr. Ford literally is
a psychology professor,

00:08:10.122 --> 00:08:14.126
you melted-down Beavis.

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:16.662
Dr. Ford's testimony was

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:18.764
so searing and so powerful
and so impressive

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:20.999
that Republicans were
clearly caught off guard.

00:08:20.999 --> 00:08:23.669
In fact, even Fox News,
the network that spends all day

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:25.137
parroting Republican
talking points,

00:08:25.137 --> 00:08:28.741
said Dr. Ford's testimony
was bad for the GOP.

00:08:28.741 --> 00:08:30.509
-The court of public opinion,

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:34.179
if our colleague is
an adequate sample of it,

00:08:34.179 --> 00:08:36.415
is that she is
extremely credible.

00:08:36.415 --> 00:08:38.884
The president cannot
be happy with this.

00:08:38.884 --> 00:08:41.353
-This was extremely emotional,

00:08:41.353 --> 00:08:45.424
extremely raw,
and extremely credible.

00:08:45.424 --> 00:08:47.826
This is a disaster
for the Republicans.

00:08:47.826 --> 00:08:50.830
-Wow. You know it's a bad when
Fox News calls it a disaster.

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:53.966
Fox News will say anything
to make Republicans feel better.

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:56.301
If the Hindenburg had been
built by Republicans,

00:08:56.301 --> 00:08:58.237
the Fox News headline
would have been this.

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:04.743
When it was Kavanaugh's turn,
he struck a much different tone

00:09:04.743 --> 00:09:06.711
from his Fox News interview
earlier this week.

00:09:06.711 --> 00:09:08.247
He was angry, defiant,

00:09:08.247 --> 00:09:10.116
and stole a page
out of Trump's playbook

00:09:10.116 --> 00:09:11.550
by claiming, with zero evidence,

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:14.386
that the allegations were part
of a left-wing conspiracy

00:09:14.386 --> 00:09:15.454
to destroy him.

00:09:15.454 --> 00:09:17.856
-Since my nomination in July,

00:09:17.856 --> 00:09:20.693
there has been
a frenzy on the left

00:09:20.693 --> 00:09:23.628
to come up with something,
anything,

00:09:23.628 --> 00:09:25.564
to block my confirmation.

00:09:25.564 --> 00:09:27.599
And millions of dollars in money

00:09:27.599 --> 00:09:30.702
from outside left-wing
opposition groups.

00:09:30.702 --> 00:09:32.637
This whole two-week effort

00:09:32.637 --> 00:09:36.742
has been a calculated
and orchestrated political hit

00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:39.477
fueled with apparent
pent-up anger

00:09:39.477 --> 00:09:41.046
about President Trump

00:09:41.046 --> 00:09:44.383
and the 2016 election,

00:09:44.383 --> 00:09:47.219
fear that has been
unfairly stoked

00:09:47.219 --> 00:09:49.488
about my judicial record,

00:09:49.488 --> 00:09:51.891
revenge on behalf
of the Clintons.

00:09:51.891 --> 00:09:53.458
-Holy [bleep], I'm surprised

00:09:53.458 --> 00:09:56.762
he didn't start attacking
George Washington.

00:09:56.762 --> 00:10:00.699
"If he's so honest,
then why does he wear a wig?"

00:10:00.699 --> 00:10:03.435
[ Laughter ]

00:10:03.435 --> 00:10:05.637
You think this was a revenge
plot by the Clintons?

00:10:05.637 --> 00:10:07.072
That's insane.

00:10:07.072 --> 00:10:10.208
Republicans always act like
they're in a slasher film

00:10:10.208 --> 00:10:12.110
and the killer
around every corner

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:14.847
is Hillary Clinton.

00:10:14.847 --> 00:10:16.749
Republicans came
into this hearing

00:10:16.749 --> 00:10:18.851
clearly trying to dismiss
and discredit Dr. Ford

00:10:18.851 --> 00:10:20.018
and instead,
they encountered someone

00:10:20.018 --> 00:10:21.153
who's immeasurable courage

00:10:21.153 --> 00:10:23.055
shone through their attempts
to obstruct.

00:10:23.055 --> 00:10:24.890
What we've seen this week
is a group of powerful men

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:25.958
trying to protect each other

00:10:25.958 --> 00:10:27.626
from the consequences
of their actions.

00:10:27.626 --> 00:10:28.961
And a woman who not only

00:10:28.961 --> 00:10:30.796
told her story with
unimaginable bravery,

00:10:30.796 --> 00:10:33.733
but also showed everyone
that she has a very large...

00:10:33.733 --> 00:10:34.966
-A-brain.

00:10:34.966 --> 00:10:36.935
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:36.935 --> 00:10:39.772
[ Cheers and applause ]

